{"v":1,"type":"session-summary","author_email":"contact@atkn.me","session":"claude:reveries-setup-audit","created_at":"2026-09-14T16:55:00Z","entries":[{"driving_event":"A setup audit found that the Reveries receive-check checked out github.sha, which is the proposal's own merge commit for pull_request events, so a pull request could modify the checker that validates it; Claude Code also did not discover the linked Skills because it reads .claude/skills rather than .agents/skills, and the linked-Skill setup lacked its ownership record and still described itself as vendored.","decision":"Check out the pull request or merge-group base SHA so the checker always runs trusted base code while proposed objects are only fetched; expose the three Skills to Claude Code through relative .claude/skills symlinks to the tracked skills root; add the symlink ownership record and replace the AGENTS.md setup paragraph with the installer's linked-Skill text.","impact":"Receive-check results can no longer be forged by editing scripts/github-receive-check.mjs or its dependencies in the proposal; changes to the checker take effect only after they reach the base branch. Claude Code sessions load using-reveries natively. A later init or remove run recognizes the linked Skills as Reveries-owned.","recurrence_control":"The receive-check workflow comment documents why github.sha must not be used; reveries doctor reports missing ownership or hooks.","alternatives":["Keep github.sha and rely on read-only token permissions","Rely only on the AGENTS.md fallback instruction for Claude Code","Vendor copies of the Skills under .claude/skills"],"sources":[{"relation":"requested-by","kind":"git-email","ref":"contact@atkn.me"}],"reveries":[],"retirements":[]}]}
